  "locked": false,
  "title": "Abort ongoing navigate events in stop loading and document.open()",
  "user": {
    "login": "noamr",
    "id": 88566,
    "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjg4NTY2",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88566?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/noamr",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "When a navigable's `ongoing navigation` is not a `navigation ID` (such as during a same-document navigation's `navigate` event dispatch, during an intercepted fragment/`pushState`/`reload`/`traverse` navigation, or before an unintercepted same-document navigation's completion microtask runs), calling `window.stop()` or `document.open()` previously did not `inform the navigation API about aborting navigation`.\n\nUpdate `stop loading` (when `unload counter` is 0) and the `document open steps` (when `node navigable` is non-null) to `inform the navigation API about aborting navigation` in the fallback branch when `ongoing navigation` is not a `navigation ID`. Also guard running the `navigate event intercept commit handler steps` on `navigateEvent` being non-null (as reached when `document.open()` runs the `URL and history update steps` after aborting or with no ongoing navigation), and remove the obsolete `ongoing navigation` ID assignment in `navigate to a fragment`.\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/65594.\n\nFixes #12247.\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Gecko (filed #12247; already implements aborting ongoing `navigate` events in `document.open()`)\n   * Chromium (already implements aborting ongoing `navigate` events in `window.stop()`)\n   * WebKit (already implements aborting ongoing `navigate` events in `window.stop()`)\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/65594\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: … (fails `signal-abort-document-open.html` and `signal-abort-window-stop-reentrant-navigateerror.html`)\n   * Gecko: … (not yet run; `nsDocShell::StopInternal` only aborts when ongoing navigation is a navigation ID, so `window.stop()` subtests are expected to fail)\n   * WebKit: … (fails `signal-abort-document-open.html`)\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: N/A\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: N/A\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13321/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 23, 2026, 4:29 PM UTC (71b413d)\">/browsing-the-web.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13321/6eac2b5...71b413d/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 23, 2026, 4:29 PM UTC (71b413d)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13321/document-lifecycle.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 23, 2026, 4:29 PM UTC (71b413d)\">/document-lifecycle.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13321/6eac2b5...71b413d/document-lifecycle.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 23, 2026, 4:29 PM UTC (71b413d)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13321/dynamic-markup-insertion.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 23, 2026, 4:29 PM UTC (71b413d)\">/dynamic-markup-insertion.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13321/6eac2b5...71b413d/dynamic-markup-insertion.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 23, 2026, 4:29 PM UTC (71b413d)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13321/nav-history-apis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 23, 2026, 4:29 PM UTC (71b413d)\">/nav-history-apis.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13321/6eac2b5...71b413d/nav-history-apis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 23, 2026, 4:29 PM UTC (71b413d)\">diff</a> )",
